  "mixed_article_sha256": "fdecf5da2e6a300e8c950c7a83016567f04d1bc79ac27e663934c4503bcf442c",
  "human_source_sentence_count": 39,
  "ai_source_sentence_count": 39,
  "alignment_unit_count": 39,
  "selected_alignment_unit_count": 12,
  "mixed_sentence_count": 39,
  "selected_ai_sentence_count": 12,
  "actual_ai_sentence_ratio": 0.307692,
  "selected_alignment_score_min": 0.330831,
  "selected_alignment_score_median": 0.54163,
  "selected_alignment_score_max": 0.955385,
  "segments": [
    {
      "sentence_index": 1,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "The postman has just left, and among the letters he delivered was one from North Wales.",
      "output_sha256": "8f58be9ef14901d5858330061d14f0c6927d739ebcd2c57876bea1a1fa1752d3",
      "alignment_unit_index": 1,
      "alignment_score": 0.790625,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        1
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "ecac6e4e3691182aa184c3d3d134ffd6c4c18b80ec5dbadb54a2a1e046d1314e"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 1,
      "source_ai_sha256": "8f58be9ef14901d5858330061d14f0c6927d739ebcd2c57876bea1a1fa1752d3",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 2,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "It was fat and soft and bulgy, and when it was opened we found it contained a bit of seaweed.",
      "output_sha256": "b0c4b45313c85eaf4fbc8464c0005ba8e09c5ab5b153ac38e30ab44f239b0dd4",
      "alignment_unit_index": 2,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 2,
      "source_human_sha256": "b0c4b45313c85eaf4fbc8464c0005ba8e09c5ab5b153ac38e30ab44f239b0dd4",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 3,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "The thought that prompted the sender was friendly, but the momentary effect was to arouse wild longings for the sea, and to add one more count to the indictment of the Kaiser, who had sent us for the holidays into the country, where we could obey the duty to economise, rather than to the seaside, where the temptations to extravagance could not be dodged.",
      "output_sha256": "333c8809513a6facc63fd72514df1d6beba46c7fa65d6d9b0f6e7f9a0e4c4e72",
      "alignment_unit_index": 3,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 3,
      "source_human_sha256": "333c8809513a6facc63fd72514df1d6beba46c7fa65d6d9b0f6e7f9a0e4c4e72",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 4,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "\"Oh, how it smells of Sheringham,\" said one whose vote is always for the East Coast.",
      "output_sha256": "141288864128d76064e46186c2bcc708313f71d9702b84781b8fa654060d2be8",
      "alignment_unit_index": 4,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 4,
      "source_human_sha256": "141288864128d76064e46186c2bcc708313f71d9702b84781b8fa654060d2be8",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 5,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "“No, this has the scent of Sidmouth, Dawlish, and Torquay,” countered another, who is enamored with the red cliffs of South Devon.",
      "output_sha256": "35dc8ebf6d2761ddf5d7129fa06ad473a6f6d97f14baddefee7db2ebb27e0b6a",
      "alignment_unit_index": 5,
      "alignment_score": 0.659304,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        5
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "295e1f47ae0e56e0d51ae8f7f37ca7ba53ae4af23a3ebc29df08ab4469522874"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 5,
      "source_ai_sha256": "35dc8ebf6d2761ddf5d7129fa06ad473a6f6d97f14baddefee7db2ebb27e0b6a",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 6,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "And so on, each finding, as he or she sniffed at the seaweed, the windows of memory opening out on to the foam of summer seas.",
      "output_sha256": "ca63ea17a3ff513761141e2c330e475ce41b4d38a2a16516a858b5c5e389e3b8",
      "alignment_unit_index": 6,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 6,
      "source_human_sha256": "ca63ea17a3ff513761141e2c330e475ce41b4d38a2a16516a858b5c5e389e3b8",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 7,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "And soon the table was enveloped in a rushing tide of recollection—memories of bathing and boating, of barefooted races on the sands, of jolly fishermen who always seemed to be looking out seaward for something that never came, of hunting for shells, and of all the careless raptures of dawn and noon and sunset by the seashore.",
      "output_sha256": "b6b6b3c3dd729da6c4fa4a219770b4f119747f318c9c2310fc54d0f92fbd3397",
      "alignment_unit_index": 7,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 7,
      "source_human_sha256": "b6b6b3c3dd729da6c4fa4a219770b4f119747f318c9c2310fc54d0f92fbd3397",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 8,
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "All awakened by the smell of a bit of seaweed.",
      "output_sha256": "7d177ca89c6195487eaaaf9a0a1d5c57a6414d4678243594483681f33f49faa3",
      "alignment_unit_index": 8,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 8,
      "source_human_sha256": "7d177ca89c6195487eaaaf9a0a1d5c57a6414d4678243594483681f33f49faa3",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 9,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "It is this magic of reminiscence that makes the world such a storehouse of intimacies and confidences.",
      "output_sha256": "07c46e5892bdf8ece9782314c790b097579add8893133b253d583b79f687dee6",
      "alignment_unit_index": 9,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 9,
      "source_human_sha256": "07c46e5892bdf8ece9782314c790b097579add8893133b253d583b79f687dee6",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 10,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "Few are the birds that sing, flowers that bloom, or clouds that drift across the azure sky that do not evoke some memory from the past, stirring us with recollection.",
      "output_sha256": "474c546171b4d957af1f48359f157239243e8fa070350774240d8c5615b9bfb1",
      "alignment_unit_index": 10,
      "alignment_score": 0.344792,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        10
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "49acf08f82ec5b2e945d1ed5a5fc95f6ef567023db9a9f167b5b6fb66b2433a5"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 10,
      "source_ai_sha256": "474c546171b4d957af1f48359f157239243e8fa070350774240d8c5615b9bfb1",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 11,
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "A chance encounter with an open drawer releases the fragrance of lavender, and with that evocative scent, the past unfurls like a scroll, bringing to life places long forgotten and voices long silent:",
      "output_sha256": "96136ba08e6738020a0be4d10f0d54f156436927e2a9b69bbcc49ad2c9a93789",
      "alignment_unit_index": 11,
      "alignment_score": 0.464052,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        11
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "69502429617fe899cb512a5b128536dbe521b703f64d6081a2a2a8f9fe0c27de"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 11,
      "source_ai_sha256": "96136ba08e6738020a0be4d10f0d54f156436927e2a9b69bbcc49ad2c9a93789",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        11
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 12,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "We tread the path their feet have worn.",
      "output_sha256": "31249132a6da1afb104305c702cd4393f419072fa3e0b1685d40727cfafbf5b0",
      "alignment_unit_index": 12,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 12,
      "source_human_sha256": "31249132a6da1afb104305c702cd4393f419072fa3e0b1685d40727cfafbf5b0",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 13,
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "We sit beneath their orchard trees, We hear, like them, the hum of bees, And rustle of the bladed corn.",
      "output_sha256": "74c8951d235a3483f7c2600b2189bb2be898ffa30103479ac18ead921662829d",
      "alignment_unit_index": 13,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 13,
      "source_human_sha256": "74c8951d235a3483f7c2600b2189bb2be898ffa30103479ac18ead921662829d",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 14,
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Who can see the first daffodils of spring without feeling a sort of spiritual festival that the beauty of the flower alone cannot explain?",
      "output_sha256": "a97fcc58ac9e9f219be0b7885cca4c681d402f0a05913c9b6cc275e61167c92a",
      "alignment_unit_index": 14,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 14,
      "source_human_sha256": "a97fcc58ac9e9f219be0b7885cca4c681d402f0a05913c9b6cc275e61167c92a",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 15,
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "The memory of all the springs of the past is in their dancing plumes, and the assurance of all the springs to come.",
      "output_sha256": "74c80816336d44a92e76eb09ce0a39d3d254b369a66309da6af524b0deb83667",
      "alignment_unit_index": 15,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 15,
      "source_human_sha256": "74c80816336d44a92e76eb09ce0a39d3d254b369a66309da6af524b0deb83667",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 16,
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "They link us up with the pageant of nature, and with the immortals of our kind—with Wordsworth watching them in \"sprightly dance\" by Ullswater, with Herrick finding in them the sweet image of the beauty and transience of life, with Shakespeare greeting them \"in the sweet o' the year\" by Avon's banks long centuries ago.",
      "output_sha256": "7c26034ee5055f25906465bfe04118c4e34c4c974038d3afa05aa88bcdf454c7",
      "alignment_unit_index": 16,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 16,
      "source_human_sha256": "7c26034ee5055f25906465bfe04118c4e34c4c974038d3afa05aa88bcdf454c7",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 17,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "And in this sensitiveness of memory to external suggestion there is infinite variety.",
      "output_sha256": "e405eef9543850060ac324cccaa992c623f936e2688a9a07b8f4d450d449cd30",
      "alignment_unit_index": 17,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 17,
      "source_human_sha256": "e405eef9543850060ac324cccaa992c623f936e2688a9a07b8f4d450d449cd30",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 18,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "It is not a collective recollection that is stirred, but rather a deeply personal one.",
      "output_sha256": "74e5d8ba3183d39537ded9e9dccd1af4d62582431a5f3d13d9d0f0b61b507cc3",
      "alignment_unit_index": 18,
      "alignment_score": 0.611429,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        18
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "c13af69c284a16e9349d7abded90486359ef5575e6d8ed9ac42d8ad91836f4e3"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 18,
      "source_ai_sha256": "74e5d8ba3183d39537ded9e9dccd1af4d62582431a5f3d13d9d0f0b61b507cc3",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        18
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 19,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "That fragment of seaweed opened numerous windows within us, each leading to unique vistas and triggering distinct, inexplicable feelings—moments that embody the innate solitude we all experience.",
      "output_sha256": "f8d8becdad867bc2ec7656d6f203820fc21fdcf4c6b13acc5779d7c7566b5a34",
      "alignment_unit_index": 19,
      "alignment_score": 0.330831,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        19
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "b9274f47fd00c94bf1ca9d83c83c8e8a8b366cffe7ea9fc9bd1a221aca41588b"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 19,
      "source_ai_sha256": "f8d8becdad867bc2ec7656d6f203820fc21fdcf4c6b13acc5779d7c7566b5a34",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        19
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 20,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Everything speaks a private language to each of us that we can never translate to others.",
      "output_sha256": "0736a3f16afcfd1d134df6b83116bc05d544014062e9aa10cfe99794cb873d49",
      "alignment_unit_index": 20,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 20,
      "source_human_sha256": "0736a3f16afcfd1d134df6b83116bc05d544014062e9aa10cfe99794cb873d49",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 21,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "I do not know what the lilac says to you; but to me it talks of a garden-gate over which it grew long ago.",
      "output_sha256": "6b1966a8ee05d279d4b1733d56ad3e61b781b29cd6926d267537a094ed245d53",
      "alignment_unit_index": 21,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 21,
      "source_human_sha256": "6b1966a8ee05d279d4b1733d56ad3e61b781b29cd6926d267537a094ed245d53",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 22,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "I am a child again, standing within the gate, and I see the red-coated soldiers marching along with jolly jests and snatching the lilac sprays from the tree as they pass.",
      "output_sha256": "a4abf4e2386852fd24634619fcb69d6116e8b51f4dfa605257d496698197d4fd",
      "alignment_unit_index": 22,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 22,
      "source_human_sha256": "a4abf4e2386852fd24634619fcb69d6116e8b51f4dfa605257d496698197d4fd",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 23,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "The emotion of pride that these heroes should honour our lilac tree by ravishing its blossoms all comes back to me, together with a flood of memories of the old garden and the old home and the vanished faces.",
      "output_sha256": "8063d0dcccc6a16374951fd4d121b164af885dde268e7bea4815296cc282966c",
      "alignment_unit_index": 23,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 23,
      "source_human_sha256": "8063d0dcccc6a16374951fd4d121b164af885dde268e7bea4815296cc282966c",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 24,
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "Why that fleeting image has remained etched in my memory, I cannot explain, yet it persists, as vivid and clear nearly fifty years later as if it were painted just yesterday, and the blooming lilac tree always brings it back to life.",
      "output_sha256": "66bf9ed6091a4cff72ba7d2828bbf3e7c0ebf865ff325a19b0133ee999d15d69",
      "alignment_unit_index": 24,
      "alignment_score": 0.560563,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        24
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "6faf88b5dee2d14195c9b5cd54ea60136fe0571a8ab905be4117de31de14df3d"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 24,
      "source_ai_sha256": "66bf9ed6091a4cff72ba7d2828bbf3e7c0ebf865ff325a19b0133ee999d15d69",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        24
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 25,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "These myriad associations enrich the tapestry of our lives, infusing it with color and poetry.",
      "output_sha256": "6009ee0dca8686b4b2d738f97060f4888c532ffd6d4b70e35571e752d522dafb",
      "alignment_unit_index": 25,
      "alignment_score": 0.338993,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        25
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "f8ffef461bbae8377f6f9c13d6d98f4faf1002c827d3d80e405f22dda92f6155"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 25,
      "source_ai_sha256": "6009ee0dca8686b4b2d738f97060f4888c532ffd6d4b70e35571e752d522dafb",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        25
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 26,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "They are the garnerings of the journey, and unlike material gains they are no burden to our backs and no anxiety to our mind.",
      "output_sha256": "070c690e2eb58c2eafe4c1d7a48173d6ffd5759c63a12eae054c6c3082a72f3f",
      "alignment_unit_index": 26,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 26,
      "source_human_sha256": "070c690e2eb58c2eafe4c1d7a48173d6ffd5759c63a12eae054c6c3082a72f3f",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 27,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "\"The true harvest of my life,\" said Thoreau, \"is something as intangible and indescribable as the tints of morning and evening.\"",
      "output_sha256": "0634419107bc8c0a3ed34a08c04aad91b8cbb0c4bed3cb40b3830147f0976854",
      "alignment_unit_index": 27,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 27,
      "source_human_sha256": "0634419107bc8c0a3ed34a08c04aad91b8cbb0c4bed3cb40b3830147f0976854",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 28,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "This encapsulates the essence of his experiences.",
      "output_sha256": "f06c2e950e2781c06d3c8477ae7d257514a6bd6e9f1a628ed3e8ee917c4b2098",
      "alignment_unit_index": 28,
      "alignment_score": 0.401765,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        28
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "266c45c699cd2e6e4bfc5d4f2d82a7f6e220eb48564d76483b136929de015e81"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 28,
      "source_ai_sha256": "f06c2e950e2781c06d3c8477ae7d257514a6bd6e9f1a628ed3e8ee917c4b2098",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        28
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 29,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "We are like bees foraging in the garden of the world, and hoarding the honey in the hive of memory.",
      "output_sha256": "34e436a5d9bb1ee54d9767b2618a0884467a4bf081a3c89e52af81707081a9ec",
      "alignment_unit_index": 29,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 29,
      "source_human_sha256": "34e436a5d9bb1ee54d9767b2618a0884467a4bf081a3c89e52af81707081a9ec",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 30,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "And no hoard is like any other hoard that ever was or ever will be.",
      "output_sha256": "41a51ee5448d480049712db66e4f4249ecd087ed7de0f0651d57f77e3ffaae72",
      "alignment_unit_index": 30,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 30,
      "source_human_sha256": "41a51ee5448d480049712db66e4f4249ecd087ed7de0f0651d57f77e3ffaae72",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 31,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "The cuckoo calling over the valley, the blackbird fluting in the low boughs in the evening, the solemn majesty of the Abbey, the life of the streets, the ebb and flow of Father Thames—everything whispers to us some secret that it has for no other ear, and touches a chord of memory that echoes in no other brain.",
      "output_sha256": "534a803b172ff4bf9a909bd751598944cb747e25bd6e06df81b37ad57251f897",
      "alignment_unit_index": 31,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 31,
      "source_human_sha256": "534a803b172ff4bf9a909bd751598944cb747e25bd6e06df81b37ad57251f897",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 32,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "Those deeps within us find only a crude expression in the vehicle of words and actions, and our intercourse with men touches but the surface of ourselves.",
      "output_sha256": "2d9b9a9f17ed06a3d4c16803c45267bce25ee465b199671b0838cc99df6bc1c0",
      "alignment_unit_index": 32,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 32,
      "source_human_sha256": "2d9b9a9f17ed06a3d4c16803c45267bce25ee465b199671b0838cc99df6bc1c0",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 33,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "The deeper feelings are “as intangible and indescribable as the tints of morning and evening.”",
      "output_sha256": "1ee638b4d4513ad5b3b04884b24ad828be859236247b5bc99bf307fae4e93ee0",
      "alignment_unit_index": 33,
      "alignment_score": 0.79658,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        33
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "1ead07463705e3981673d5276cb5baddfac54ba149905a0d705a93662384439f"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 33,
      "source_ai_sha256": "1ee638b4d4513ad5b3b04884b24ad828be859236247b5bc99bf307fae4e93ee0",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        33
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 34,
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "It was one of the most companionable of men, William Morris, who said:",
      "output_sha256": "b79d5e3b7073633759fa61d8188198a89c08f517b7a1d871de23d4be244a1243",
      "alignment_unit_index": 34,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 34,
      "source_human_sha256": "b79d5e3b7073633759fa61d8188198a89c08f517b7a1d871de23d4be244a1243",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 35,
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "That God has made each one of us as lone As He Himself sits.",
      "output_sha256": "17047d52b3849c98a11233174f1872968800e601d6e5f1f384c487c1a5ada280",
      "alignment_unit_index": 35,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 35,
      "source_human_sha256": "17047d52b3849c98a11233174f1872968800e601d6e5f1f384c487c1a5ada280",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 36,
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "That is why, in moments of exaltation, our only refuge is silence, and the world of memory within answers the world of suggestion without.",
      "output_sha256": "1096e4dc808ba401d3ee3a805b529800dfe1f06175830de07a42e37cdbf461b1",
      "alignment_unit_index": 36,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 36,
      "source_human_sha256": "1096e4dc808ba401d3ee3a805b529800dfe1f06175830de07a42e37cdbf461b1",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 37,
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "“What does the seaweed remind you of?” someone inquired as I emerged from my reverie after inhaling its fragrance.",
      "output_sha256": "2b301a268ff5e05c90d768523cd382a7674162f28ca4ced6f5355ae99951ce73",
      "alignment_unit_index": 37,
      "alignment_score": 0.522697,
      "human_sentence_indices": [
        37
      ],
      "human_sha256": [
        "5620f8f4bf6fd7b21bb499a341b15153879307d4fe7687e456f75d981c9c8308"
      ],
      "source_ai_sentence_index": 37,
      "source_ai_sha256": "2b301a268ff5e05c90d768523cd382a7674162f28ca4ced6f5355ae99951ce73",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": [
        37
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 38,
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "origin": "human",
      "text": "\"It reminds me,\" I said, \"of all the seas that wash our shores, and of all the brave sailors who are guarding these seas day and night, while we sit here secure.",
      "output_sha256": "746ff07176a6ad71ea588d1ca0b605ab9226f6262cd1658e4003c7aaaf76b7e7",
      "alignment_unit_index": 38,
      "alignment_score": null,
      "source_human_sentence_index": 38,
      "source_human_sha256": "746ff07176a6ad71ea588d1ca0b605ab9226f6262cd1658e4003c7aaaf76b7e7",
      "ai_unit_sentence_indices": []
    },
    {
      "sentence_index": 39,
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "origin": "ai",
      "text": "It also reminds me that I have an article to write, and its title is 'A Bit of Seaweed.'”",
      "output_sha256": "955aec0f3f1a04da22fa207fd470ad1d29094ab9559641347f500117abd615ff",
      "alignment_unit_index": 39,
      "alignment_score": 0.955385,
